<section>
  <div class="container content">
    <h2>Gold Mining in Nevada</h2>
    <p>Nevada leads the United States in gold production. The headlines belong to the giant hardrock mines along the Carlin Trend, but the state's placer ground has supported small and mid-size miners for more than 150 years. Dry desert washes, ancient buried river channels, and gravel benches across the Great Basin still hold recoverable gold &mdash; much of it fine, which is exactly what a properly built wash plant is designed to capture.</p>
    <p>The real challenge in Nevada is water, not gold. Most placer ground sits far from a year-round creek, so successful operations recirculate. Every wash plant we build for Nevada is configured to run on a closed settling-pond system, which lets you work claims that would be impossible with a setup that needs constant fresh water. Our <a href="/blog/gold-wash-plant-water-requirements/">water requirements guide</a> walks through how to plan a recirculation system.</p>
    <p>Whether you are testing a new claim near Winnemucca or scaling a commercial operation around Battle Mountain, we match the plant to your yardage, water budget, and ground conditions. See our <a href="/blog/choosing-right-size-gold-wash-plant/">wash plant sizing guide</a> or the <a href="/blog/gold-wash-plant-cost-guide/">cost guide</a> to plan your build.</p>
  </div>
</section>

