    <h2>Why Our Wash Plants Work in Nevada</h2>
    <p>Nevada placer mining rewards equipment built for dry-region conditions. Every plant we ship into the state is configured for the realities of Great Basin ground:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Closed-circuit water recirculation</strong> as standard, so you can mine far from any creek</li>
      <li><strong>Aggressive scrubbing</strong> that breaks apart caliche-cemented desert gravels to free trapped gold</li>
      <li><strong>Fine-gold recovery to 200 mesh</strong> &mdash; Nevada placer gold runs fine, and our sluice design is built to hold it</li>
      <li><strong>Year-round operation</strong> with no freeze-up across most of the state</li>
      <li><strong>Fast 30-minute setup</strong> so you can test several claims in a single season</li>
      <li><strong>Diesel power options</strong> for off-grid BLM ground with no utility access</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Not sure how much gold your ground needs to hold to be worth mining? Our <a href="/blog/gold-per-yard-profitability/">gold-per-yard profitability guide</a> covers the break-even math.</p>
